<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guy II of Blois</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1397">1397</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Guy II of Châtillon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Guy II was the last count of Blois of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-chatillon">House of Châtillon</a>, ruling from 1381. Heavily in debt and left without an heir after the death of his son, he sold the county in 1391 to Louis, Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orleans">Orléans</a>, brother of Charles VI, who took possession at Guy's death in 1397. Blois thus passed to the Orléans branch of the royal family and later to the crown.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/guy-ii-of-blois.jpg" alt="Guy II of Blois" width="320" height="434" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jacques de Boucq · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Guy_II_of_Blois-Chatillon.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
